Hyphens, dashes, slashes and pipes respond more after words than after
arithmetic signs or whitespace. Hyphens after single-letter variables are
weaker than after full words. Separator responses are also stronger near the
start of a document; that extra response decays with position. Other tokens
are left quiet. Only a short text suffix and document position are carried.
